 "notes": [
  "Voila audit of 26,646 Voila rows in the Hammer product list (judged from names/units only; no prices seen). The current matcher links 1,343 Voila products to catalogue items. I kept 313 as legit, put 313 in assignments and excluded 1030.",
  "Exclusions cover: wrong pack size (about 211), variants (flavoured, organic, lactose-free, plant-based, light, no-salt, crunchy, brown/other types, ~690), non-grocery or prepared foods that only share a keyword (tea, gum, bakery, sausages, pasta bowls, dog food), multipacks of small units, and per-kg produce sold by the each or by 1.36 kg bag.",
  "Per-kg catalogue items (bananas, apples, pears, grapes, roma/vine tomatoes, broccoli, navel oranges, cabbage, sweet potatoes, zucchini, red onions) have no assignments: Voila lists them as '1 Count' or 1.36 kg bags, so a pack price would be read as a price per kg. Needs price-per-kg normalisation in the matcher or the raw price rows.",
  "No legit Voila product found for: eggs-medium-12, mozzarella-340g (only ball/shredded/other sizes), greek-yogurt-plain (only flavoured, organic or high-protein), pita-6 (5-packs), sugar-4kg, pineapple-each, green-onions-each, garlic-each, avocados-4 (organic only), blueberries-510g (170/340 g only), ginger-kg.",
  "73 legit products fail the strict matcher, so they are not in assignments (matcher gap, not data): e.g. 2% milk (the 'skim' conflict word hits 'Partly Skimmed'), multigrain bread 600 g, bagels/English muffins/buns/rolls/croissants/tortillas with pack counts, coffee, kidney beans, chick peas, McIntosh apple juice, red/green peppers 'Extra Large', white mushrooms. They are left out of exclude so the matcher can still pick them up if it is fixed.",
  "Packs within 8%% of catalogue size were accepted (e.g. 946 ml broth, 1.75 L plant milk vs 1.89 L, 427 g margarine, 2.84 L oil, 500 ml maple syrup). Fresh brown eggs, omega-3, free-run, organic, extra large and jumbo were treated as different variants of 'Large eggs'."
 ]
